First, sorry I was off mark with my first guess. That "inode" should be a path. So it's trying to write to "mapred". I doubt that's correct -- first of all I am not sure what a relative path would mean in this context. I would double check your mapred-site.xml configuration file, maybe take a look at this http://bugcy013.blogspot.com/2012/12/hadoop-mapreduce-job-submission.html (but we don't support Hadoop and you should do what's right for your distribution and setting). Also, if you could try to launch a Mapreduce job outside R, that would confirm this is not an rmr2 problem, as I suspect.

Antonio

